menu "ESP SR Demo Configuration"

    config ESP_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default "YourWiFiSSID"
        help
            SSID (network name) the board should connect to. Only used as a
            factory-default fallback -- see the config portal note below.

    config ESP_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi Password"
        default "YourWiFiPassword"
        help
            WPA2 password for the WiFi network above.

    config VOICE_ASSISTANT_ENDPOINT_URL
        string "Voice assistant HTTP endpoint URL"
        default "http://192.168.1.100:8000/talk"
        help
            HTTP endpoint the board POSTs recorded audio to after hearing
            the wake word (mono, 16-bit PCM, 16kHz WAV), and reads a spoken
            response back from (raw mono 16-bit PCM, 16kHz, no header).
            See README.md for the full contract.

            This is only the factory-default value baked into the first
            boot. Both this and the WiFi SSID/password above can be changed
            later, without reflashing, via the config portal (see
            PORTAL_AP_SSID_PREFIX below) -- whatever was last saved there
            takes priority over these Kconfig defaults.

    config PORTAL_AP_SSID_PREFIX
        string "Config portal AP SSID prefix"
        default "ESP32-Setup"
        help
            If the board can't connect to WiFi within the connect timeout,
            it brings up an open access point named "<prefix>-XXXX" (last
            two bytes of the AP MAC) alongside its normal retry attempts.
            Join that AP and browse to http://192.168.4.1/ to enter a new
            WiFi SSID/password and/or a new voice assistant endpoint URL;
            saving reboots the board with the new settings.

endmenu
